.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-payments-release - Release a payment after expiry (prepare, sign, and broadcast)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 payments release  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Prepare the transaction that calls release() on the RAIL0 contract.

.PP
Release is only available after authorizationExpiry has passed on-chain.
Returns the remaining (uncaptured) escrowed balance to the payer. Permissionless
— both payer and payee can call it; the caller is whoever the signing key belongs
to (derived from the key), so pass the payer's key to release as the payer.
The API returns 202 immediately; poll 'payments get \&'. The status
advances to "released" only on a TOTAL release (an untouched authorization,
nothing captured); if a capture left a refundable residual the status stays
unchanged and that residual remains refundable.

.PP
Pass --private-key (-p): the CLI signs locally and broadcasts in one step.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for release

.PP
\fB-p\fP, \fB--private-key\fP=""
	Caller's secp256k1 private key (0x-prefixed hex); signs and broadcasts in one step

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=2m0s
	Max time to wait when --wait is set

.PP
\fB-w\fP, \fB--wait\fP[=false]
	Block until the operation confirms on-chain (or fails)

.PP
\fB-y\fP, \fB--yes\fP[=false]
	Skip the confirmation prompt (required to run non-interactively)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  # Payee releases
  rail0 payments release 0xrail0Id… -p 0xPayeeKey…

  # Payer releases (just use the payer's key)
  rail0 payments release 0xrail0Id… -p 0xPayerKey…
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0-payments(1)\fP
